  "description": {
    "rendered": "<div style=\"width: 3840px;\" class=\"wp-video\"><video class=\"wp-video-shortcode\" id=\"video-849432-1\" width=\"3840\" height=\"2160\" preload=\"metadata\" controls=\"controls\"><source type=\"video/mp4\" src=\"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/iss072e503021-aurora-borealis-4k.mp4?_=1\" /><a href=\"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/iss072e503021-aurora-borealis-4k.mp4\">https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/iss072e503021-aurora-borealis-4k.mp4</a></video></div>\n<p>Brilliant green auroras glow and swirl above clusters of the white lights of cities on Earth as viewed from space at night. Part of the view is blocked by a circular piece of equipment and part of a capsule docked to the International Space Station.</p>\n"
  },
  "caption": {
    "rendered": "<p>https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/iss072e503021-aurora-borealis-4k.mp4 Brilliant green auroras glow and swirl above clusters of the white lights of cities on Earth as viewed from space at night. Part of the view is blocked by a circular piece of equipment and part of a capsule docked to the International Space Station.</p>\n"
